Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:49:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 24/31] EPA: grow the horizon from the closest face; size its
 buffer from ccd_iterations

The horizon scan tests every polytope face on its own. When the support point w lies, to rounding, on the planes of several faces, it deletes faces that are not connected to the closest face (two regions touching at a vertex, or a ring), so the horizon is not one loop, the attached faces do not close the polytope, and the edge list can outgrow its fixed 24 entries: EPA then returned no face and the heightfield pair lost its contact for the step (OverflowType.EPA_HORIZON). Isaac's G1 foot meshes on the rough-terrain heightfield with Isaac Lab 3.0's 1 cm geom gap hit it a few times per 4096-world PPO iteration (rough_il3): in the three states captured on Metal, EPA ran 33-39 iterations on the inflated shapes of prisms whose cores were 0.1-0.8 mm apart (the next commit takes those off EPA).

MuJoCo C deletes only the visible faces connected to the closest face (horizon / horizonRec). The scan is kept; when its horizon is not one simple loop it is undone (its faces carry a per-iteration mark in face_norm2, unused for deleted faces) and the deleted region grows from the closest face by passes over the face list, adding a visible face only when it shares an edge with the region. A scan whose horizon is one loop is used as before, so results are bitwise unchanged there (static sets: all but 2-7 of 40000 worlds, every one a non-loop horizon; the heightfield contact checks bitwise).

The horizon buffer now holds every edge of EPA's largest polytope, 3 (5 + ccd_iterations) - 6 (114 at 35). If it still fills, or the region is still not a disk, EPA returns its closest face (a lower bound on the depth) instead of no contact; a full buffer still sets EPA_HORIZON. As MuJoCo C, EPA also stops with its closest face when the new faces would not fit the face buffer, instead of failing in _attach_face and returning no contact (1 in 40000 G1 foot placements).

test_box_box_horizon: 5 edges now suffice for its configuration (the scan needed 8); 4 overflow and keep the contact.
